/* book exam traps: Counting each pair twice: 12 units need 66 point-to-point links, not 132. The 132 is the number of link ends. | A signal is not a message: one message usually carries several signals, so "one wire per signal" becomes "one message for several signals", not one message per signal. | High bandwidth is not determinism. A fast bus can still have an unknown worst-case delay if messages queue; determinism means the worst case is guaranteed. | Bus load uses the period of each message, not the number of messages alone: 20 messages every 10 ms load the bus twice as much as 20 messages every 20 ms. | A gateway is not a junction box: it is an ECU that decides which messages cross, and it can change their rate or format. */
