/* book exam traps: CAN is not a seven-layer stack. The CAN standard covers layers 1 and 2 only; transport (ISO-TP) and application (UDS, OBD) are separate standards. | Master-slave is an organization, not a topology. LIN is master-slave on a bus topology; a star is a wiring shape. | CAN does not use CSMA/CD. In CSMA/CD a collision destroys both frames; in CAN the higher-priority frame wins the clash without damage. | SAE defines Classes A, B and C. Name C+ or D as a textbook extension for buses above 1 Mbit/s, and say which buses you mean. | A single ring is not fault tolerant: one broken fibre in a MOST ring stops the whole ring. */
